to examine a work of fiction

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.000
to tell you all of the
laws that it has broken.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.390
So without further ado let's dig in

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.503
to Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.110
- [Charlie] Hi Mr. Jopeck.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.593
- [Mr. Jopeck] Ah, come
along Charlie you're late.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.480
- [Charlie] It's pay day Mr. Jopeck.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:40.430
- [Mr. Jopeck] You're
right, there you are.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:41.263
- Thanks.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.920
- Say hello to your Grandpa Joe.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:44.760
- Okay.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.480
- Okay big problem right off the bat.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.020
Charlie is way too young
to have a paper route.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.520
I think this is a child labor violation.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.370
Here this is governed by

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.560
the Federal Labor Standards Act or FLSA

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.300
which states that no
one under the age of 14

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.920
can hold a job in the United States.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.480
So later on in this movie,
Mike TV actually mentions

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.450
that he's 12 years old.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.790
And because I think all the children

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.290
are supposed to be exactly the same age

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.320
I think Charlie is clearly
under the age of 14.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.730
Therefore while Mr. Jopeck here

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.360
may be thinking he is doing a good thing

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.760
he's actually committing
a child labor violation.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.690
♪ Oompa Loompa do ba dee doo ♪

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:21.523
- What's happening?

00:02:21.523 --> 00:02:22.790
- Willy Wonka's opening his factory.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.070
He's gonna let people in.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:24.919
- You sure?

00:02:24.919 --> 00:02:25.752
- It's on the radio

00:02:25.752 --> 00:02:27.626
and he's giving truckloads
of chocolate away.

00:02:27.626 --> 00:02:28.585
- [Teacher] Class dismissed!

00:02:28.585 --> 00:02:30.973
- [Boy] No, no it's only for five people.

00:02:30.973 --> 00:02:31.806
- Class undismissed.

00:02:31.806 --> 00:02:33.690
- He's hidden five golden tickets

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.960
and the people who find
'em will win the big prize.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.220
- Where's he hidden the tickets?

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.053
- Inside five Wonka Bars.

00:02:38.053 --> 00:02:39.780
You gotta buy Wonka Bars to find 'em.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.570
- [Teacher] Class redismissed!

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.590
- Okay big problem here.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.300
This is a clear violation
of sweepstakes law

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.060
that exists in most states.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.500
You might notice that whenever
you see a giveaway on TV

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.430
there's always some fine print that says

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.830
no purchase necessary.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.200
There is a very, very
good reason for that.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.820
The reason is, if you require purchase

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.530
you're no longer a free
giveaway in a sweepstakes

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.280
you are an illegal lottery.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.830
That's the difference
between gambling in a lottery

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.080
and a sweepstakes which
is just a giveaway.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.790
That's why you always hear
that no purchase is necessary

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.940
and you can participate in the giveaway

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.030
without actually making a purchase.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.270
Willy Wonka has not added that language

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:20.950
and he explicitly requires
you to buy his chocolate bars

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.730
in order to participate
in the golden ticket hunt.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.930
That is a clear violation
of sweepstakes law

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.240
and my guess is that
he would be on the hook

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.320
for the millions of dollars
that people have spent

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.660
buying Wonka Bars in order to participate

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.690
in this particular sweepstakes.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:38.302
♪ If you're not greedy you will go far ♪

00:03:38.302 --> 00:03:39.790
- I want it now!

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.487
What's the matter with
those twerps down there?

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.280
- For five days now the
entire flipping factory's

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.420
been on the job.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.290
They haven't shelled a
peanut in there since Monday.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.440
They've been shelling
flaming chocolate bars

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.914
from dawn to dusk.

00:03:51.914 --> 00:03:53.463
- Make 'em work nights!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.160
- Come along, come along you girls.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.360
Put a jerk in it or
you'll be out on your ears

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.240
every one of ya!

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.490
And listen to this!

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.000
The first girl that finds a golden ticket

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.020
gets a one pound bonus in your pay packet!

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.043
What do you think of that?

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:14.480
- Alright that is another FLSA violation.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.460
He is clearly pushing his
staff far, far too hard.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.280
They're working for five days straight

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.830
form dawn until dusk.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.490
He's making them work overtime

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.550
without paying them anything extra.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:25.710
That is a clear violation.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.450
That's called a wage and hour violation.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.750
I have friends who specialize

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.470
in these kind of wage and hour violations

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.700
under the FLSA.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.380
And they will tell you that the
damages in this kind of case

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.380
really, really start to add up

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.390
because not only do you
have to pay them back pay

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.930
for all the extra work that they have done

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.880
but you're probably gonna
have to pay them overtime.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.630
And on top of it you're
gonna pay statutory damages.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.290
So for the thousands of workers

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.390
that this man has in his factory

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.580
he's gonna be on the hook

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.800
for hundreds of thousands
if not millions of dollars

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.630
in wage and hour violations.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:55.534
Not good.

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:59.270
♪ Oompa Loompa do ba dee dee ♪

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.350
- May I introduce myself?

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.060
Oslo Slugworth,

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.460
president of Slugworth
Chocolates, Incorporated.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.490
Now listen carefully

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:10.580
because I'm going to make
you very rich indeed.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.730
Mr. Wonka is at this moment
working on a fantastic invention

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:16.463
the Everlasting Gobstopper.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.040
If he succeeds he'll ruin me.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.680
So all I want you to do is to get hold

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.506
of just one Everlasting Gobstopper

00:05:23.506 --> 00:05:27.210
and bring it to me so that I
can find the secret formula.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:30.700
Your reward will be 10,000 of these.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.550
- Alright, so what Slugworth
is trying to do here

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.800
is engage in corporate espionage,

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.480
basically trying to steal a trade secret.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:40.500
If the gobstopper had
been publicly released

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.760
then there would be nothing
that could stop Slugworth

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:43.970
from just simply buying one

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:46.770
and trying to reverse engineer
the Everlasting Gobstopper.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.870
However since the Everlasting Gobstopper

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.360
has not been publicly released

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.770
it still probably qualifies

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:54.290
as a trade secret under Willy Wonka.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.250
So by asking Charlie to find
an Everlasting Gobstopper

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.670
and bring it back to Slugworth

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.630
he's essentially asking Charlie
to engage in a conspiracy

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.040
to commit a trade secrets violation.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.097
Now I know everyone's going to say,

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:07.510
"But Slugworth actually
works for Willy Wonka."

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.950
But here's the thing,

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.570
a conspiracy can have different mens rea

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.190
for different members of the conspiracy.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.350
That's how you have a police officer

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.140
who engages in a conspiracy

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.600
who's not guilty of the conspiracies

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.520
all the other co-conspirators.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.070
So you might get a weird situation

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:24.790
where Charlie has violated
the trade secrets act

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.310
by engaging in this conspiracy

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.442
while Slugworth has not.

00:06:28.442 --> 00:06:31.720
♪ Oompa Loompa do ba da dee ♪

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:35.330
- Now, will the children
kindly step up here?

00:06:42.355 --> 00:06:44.120
(man mumbling)

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.640
- [Man] Floods, fire, frost or frippery.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.240
- [Mike TV] Accident,
what kinda accidents?

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.770
- [Woman] I didn't know
we had to sign anything

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:51.790
for this to work.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.240
- [Violet] I can't see
what it says in the bottom.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.080
- Violet, you first.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.380
Sign here.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.300
- Hold it.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.500
Let me through here, you kids.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.960
Violet baby, don't you
sign anything there.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.430
What's this all about?

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.100
- Standard form of contract.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.650
- Don't talk to me about
contracts Wonka I use 'em myself,

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.070
they're strictly for suckers.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.570
- Yes, but you wouldn't
begrudge me a little protection.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.580
A drop.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.210
- I don't sign anything without my lawyer.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:14.340
- [Mr. Salt] My Veruca
don't sign anything either.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.280
- Then she don't go in.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.370
I'm sorry, rules of the house.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.280
- Okay, so Willy Wonka is
trying to get the children

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:22.080
to sign a liability waiver

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.240
to limit how much exposure he has

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.320
when things go terribly, terribly wrong.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.130
Now, I probably don't
need to tell you that

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.450
if you can't physically read the contract

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.740
that's going to be problematic

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.930
for the person that's trying
to disclaim the liability.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.100
That's called an unconscionable contract

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.700
that there is some procedural
or structural problem

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:39.980
with the contract itself

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.790
that makes it unconscionable
for the courts to enforce.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.220
And if you can't physically see

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.280
the tiny print at the
bottom of this contract

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:49.230
that is a textbook
unconscionable contract.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.500
But on top of that, Willy
Wonka's gonna have some problems

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:54.390
with signing a contract
with these children.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:55.940
Only the children here have signed them.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:56.970
They are minors.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.770
The parents, while they are present

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.640
are not the ones signing this contract.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:03.450
When a child signs a
contract, generally speaking,

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:07.340
that contract is voidable
at the option of the minor.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.630
On top of that this contract
seems to be complete gibberish.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.100
Generally speaking with
a limitation on liability

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.450
you can disclaim things like negligence

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.790
but you can almost never
disclaim recklessness.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.950
This contract doesn't
appear to do any of that.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.230
Maybe that's in the fine
print that no one can see.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.640
But it appears to be just a
string of legal sounding words

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.880
that don't actually have any real meaning.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.220
So I'm gonna go out on a limb

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.960
and say that Willy
Wonka has not disclaimed

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:31.970
any of his liability

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:34.860
and he's going to have
problems with civil suits

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.277
later on down the line for his
negligence and recklessness.

00:08:38.277 --> 00:08:42.960
♪ What do you think will come of that ♪

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.480
- [Woman] What are they doing there?

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.450
- [Willy Wonka] Must be
creaming and sugaring time.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:48.330
- [Violet] Well they can't be real people.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.040
- [Willy Wonka] Well of
course they're real people.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:50.980
- [Man] Stuff a nonsense.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.906
- [Willy Wonka] No, Oompa Loompas.

00:08:52.906 --> 00:08:54.538
- [Group] Oompa Loompas?

00:08:54.538 --> 00:08:55.494
- [Willy Wonka] From Loompaland.

00:08:55.494 --> 00:08:57.260
- Loompaland, there's no such place.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.093
- Excuse me dear lady.

00:08:58.093 --> 00:09:00.400
- Mr. Wonka, I am a teacher of geography.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:01.880
- Oh, well then you now all about it

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.810
and what a terrible country it is.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.410
Nothing but desolate
wastes and fierce beasts.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.660
And the poor little Oompa Loompas

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.290
were so small and helpless

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.400
they would get gobbled up right and left.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.740
A Wangdoodle would eat
10 of them for breakfast

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.940
and think nothing of it.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:21.560
So I said, come and live
with me in peace and safety

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.491
away from all the
Wangdoodles and Hornswagglers

00:09:24.491 --> 00:09:28.340
and Snozzwangers and
rotten Vermicious Knids.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:31.080
- Snozzwangers, Vermicious Knids?

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.400
What kind of rubbish is that?

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.240
- I'm sorry but all questions
must be submitted in writing.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.110
And so in the greatest of secrecy

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.860
I transported the entire
population of Oompa Loompas

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.760
to my factory here.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.540
- Okay, so what Willy
Wonka has admitted here

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.020
is a huge immigration violation.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.130
He says that he secretly
transported the entire population

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:54.540
of a separate country, of
Loompaland to his factory.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:55.390
A lot of problems here.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.710
Number one, I don't see any reasonable way

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:00.620
he could have transported
an entire country

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.510
legally through immigration channels.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:03.880
On the other hand it sounds like

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:06.730
the Oompa Loompas were really
facing quite a hardship

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:07.900
in their native country.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.040
So conceivably they
could have been refugees

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.180
seeking asylum in the
United States or the U.K.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:16.260
Which actually might have
allowed it to go through.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.380
But I don't get the sense from Willy Wonka

